.TH ARCHAIC-HELPER 1 "May 2026" "Archaic 0.9.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
archaic-helper \- persistent connection helper for the Archaic autocomplete daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B archaic-helper
.RI [ socket_path ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B archaic-helper
maintains a persistent Unix domain socket connection to the Archaic daemon.
It reads commands from stdin and writes responses to stdout, eliminating
the overhead of socket setup for each query. This is what the Fish shell
plugin uses internally for fast completions.
.SH USAGE
Start the helper, optionally specifying the daemon socket path:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ archaic-helper
$ archaic-helper /tmp/archaic-daemon.sock
.fi
.RE
.PP
Then pipe commands via stdin:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ echo "complete /path 20" | archaic-helper
.fi
.RE
.SH COMMANDS
Commands are sent one per line via stdin:
.TP
.B complete \fIprefix\fR [\fIlimit\fR] [\fIcwd\fR] [\fIdirs_only\fR] [\fIcommand\fR]
Get path completions for the given prefix. CWD boosts nearby paths.
.TP
.B fuzzy \fIprefix\fR [\fIlimit\fR]
Get fuzzy path completions matching the prefix pattern.
.TP
.B suggest \fIprefix\fR [\fIcwd\fR]
Get the single best suggestion for the given prefix.
.TP
.B query \fIcwd\fR \fIinput\fR
Validate a path. Returns existence, type, and full path.
.TP
.B ping
Check if the daemon is running. Returns uptime in milliseconds.
.TP
.B metrics
Display daemon performance metrics and statistics.
.TP
.B scan-status
Check the current scan progress and status.
.TP
.B quit / exit
Terminate the helper process.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ARCHAIC_CONFIG
Path to configuration file (default: ~/.config/archaic/config.toml).
.TP
.B ARCHAIC_SOCKET
Path to daemon socket (default: /tmp/archaic-daemon.sock).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/archaic/config.toml
User configuration file.
.TP
.I /etc/archaic/config.toml
System-wide configuration file.
.TP
.I /tmp/archaic-daemon.sock
Default daemon socket path.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Get completions for a path prefix:
.RS
.nf
$ echo "complete ~/pro 10" | archaic-helper
D ~/projects
F ~/profile.txt
.fi
.RE
.PP
Check daemon health:
.RS
.nf
$ echo "ping" | archaic-helper
12345678
.fi
.RE
.PP
Get the best suggestion:
.RS
.nf
$ echo "suggest ~/doc" | archaic-helper
~/documents
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR archaic (1),
.BR archaic-cli (1),
.BR archaic.conf (5)
